OBJECTS 6
"arrival.underkeep.upper-stair" ARRIVAL_POINT 2 2 0 "Upper Stair Arrival" "Arrival from the Gatehouse." 0 1 "" ""
"note.underkeep.masons" NOTE 3 2 0 "Mason's Warning" "We sealed the old hall, but every morning the mortar is wet on the inside." 0 0 "" ""
"recruit.underkeep.elska" RECRUIT 6 7 1 "Elska" "Elska lowers her spear. 'I know a way through. I will not take it alone.'" 2001 0 "" ""
"party.underkeep.camp" PARTY_MANAGEMENT 7 7 0 "Underkeep Camp" "Choose which recruited companions travel with you." 0 0 "" ""
"corpse.underkeep.mason" CORPSE 12 12 0 "The Last Mason" "Stone dust fills the dead mason's mouth. His hammer points toward the sealed stair." 0 0 "" ""
"transition.underkeep.ascent" LEVEL_TRANSITION 13 13 0 "Return to the Gatehouse" "The stair climbs toward the abandoned watch." 0 0 "gatehouse.level-1" "arrival.gatehouse.lower-gate"
ROOMS 3
"room.underkeep.entry" 1 1 6 5 "The Weeping Stair" "Confirm that the campaign has moved into a persistent second place." "Cold descent" "Water has run upward along these walls since the breach." "Dislocation"
"room.underkeep.camp" 1 7 12 3 "The Survivor's Camp" "Introduce recruitment and active-party management." "Guarded relief" "One survivor kept a lamp burning for those who might follow." "Earned companionship"
"room.underkeep.seal" 8 10 7 5 "The Broken Seal" "Return the party to the Gatehouse while preserving what happened here." "Uneasy resolve" "The builders did not construct this threshold. They built around it." "Forward pull"
TRIGGERS 4
"trigger.underkeep.arrival" ENTER_ROOM 1 1 "room.underkeep.entry" 1 "The stair closes behind you with the sound of a distant stone door."
"trigger.underkeep.note" INTERACT_OBJECT 3 2 "note.underkeep.masons" 1 "The final line was carved with a chisel: DO NOT LET IT LEARN YOUR NAME."
"trigger.underkeep.recruit" INTERACT_OBJECT 6 7 "recruit.underkeep.elska" 1 "Elska joins the reserve roster. The camp now serves as a party-management point."
"trigger.underkeep.seal" ENTER_ROOM 8 10 "room.underkeep.seal" 1 "Behind the broken seal, the stone bears tool marks older than the keep above."
END
